VARIANT COMPARISON (bias state vs process-noise inflation)
* inflation variant: lag-1 residual autocorr = +0.3721, mean = +0.0333
* bias variant     : lag-1 residual autocorr = +0.3217, mean = +0.0306
* WINNER: 'bias' - smaller |lag-1 autocorrelation| (and smaller
  |mean| as tie-break) of the per-step bearing residual series, i.e.
  the more innovation-white / consistent filter. Rationale: white
  residuals indicate the filter's process/measurement models have
  absorbed the systematic effects; persistent autocorrelation would
  indicate unmodeled structure (drift or unmodeled dynamics).

